  {
   "t": 0,
   "text": "The hardest thing in defending is not pressing yet, and this teaches it.",
   "hold": 2.5,
   "beat": "hook"
  },
  {
   "t": 0,
   "text": "A compact block sits behind a pressing line marked across the middle.",
   "hold": 2.5,
   "beat": "picture"
  },
  {
   "t": 3.15,
   "text": "Nobody moves until the trigger. A pass into a wide area, or someone turned backwards.",
   "hold": 2.5,
   "beat": "action"
  },
  {
   "t": 12.79,
   "text": "Then everyone jumps together, because a lone presser is worse than none at all.",
   "hold": 2.5,
   "beat": "action"
  },
  {
   "t": 19.68,
   "text": "Reset the block after every attack, and change the trigger without telling them.",
   "hold": 2.5,
   "beat": "progression"
  },
  {
   "t": 22.18,
   "text": "Holding the block is harder than the sprint, and this is where they learn it.",
